        "apps/n8n-lego/test/lego-skill.test.mjs"
      ],
      "notes": "Skill = procedural knowledge + rules + procedure + capability map + validators. The REGISTRY is implemented; skills stay declarative documents and nothing executes a procedure. FOUR published operations only. register/select/load/release are internal lifecycle methods of the registry object, deliberately NOT published caller operations: publishing load would make lazy discovery a caller concern, and publishing register would let a caller mutate the vocabulary other consumers negotiate against. There is no execute operation and no ai:skill:execute permission — execution is not a skill operation, so no published name may imply it. A skill DECLARES requiredCapabilities and never grants them; the capability system stays the sole authority. validate-selection checks the DECLARATION, never the caller's authorization. An unknown capability fails closed. Locked in P2.12 finalize by XA-19; XA-11 (whether Skill ultimately belongs under ai-foundation) remains open-for-manager and is a separate architecture decision that this lock does not settle."
    },
